<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <actionCalls>
        <description>Asks whether the link value belongs to a Contact or Lead. Returns only true or false (ADR 0002). Legacy record Id links count only when the setup allows them.</description>
        <name>Check_Link_Exists</name>
        <label>Check Link Exists</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <actionName>PublicIdExistsInvocable</actionName>
        <actionType>apex</actionType>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Does_Link_Exist</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <faultConnector>
            <isGoTo>true</isGoTo>
            <targetReference>screenConfirmation</targetReference>
        </faultConnector>
        <flowTransactionModel>CurrentTransaction</flowTransactionModel>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>linkValue</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>linkValue</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <nameSegment>PublicIdExistsInvocable</nameSegment>
        <offset>0</offset>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </actionCalls>
    <apiVersion>68.0</apiVersion>
    <areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>false</areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>
    <decisions>
        <description>A link that matches no Contact or Lead creates no Request. With type-in mode on, the Recipient can type an address instead. Otherwise the Recipient sees the success page, so the page can&apos;t be used to test which links exist.</description>
        <name>Does_Link_Exist</name>
        <label>Does Link Exist</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Allow_Type_In</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No match</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Link_Exists</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Check_Link_Exists.linkExists</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Quick_UnsubscribeDecision</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Link exists</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Checks whether type-in mode is on in the Unsubscribe Link Setup record.</description>
        <name>Allow_Type_In</name>
        <label>Allow Type-In</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <isGoTo>true</isGoTo>
            <targetReference>screenConfirmation</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No type-in</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Type_In_Allowed</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Unsubscribe_Link_Setup.Enable_Type_in_Email_Address__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Yes</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Blank_Values_Flow</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Type-in allowed</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Checks if the confirmation screen is enabled and skips it if not.</description>
        <name>Quick_UnsubscribeDecision</name>
        <label>Quick Unsubscribe</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Are_you_sure</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Include screen 1</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Skip_screen_1</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Unsubscribe_Link_Setup.Confirmation_Page__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>No</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Create_Link_Request</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Skip screen 1</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Customer facing flow of the Unsubscribe Link managed package from AppExchange. It runs as the site guest user.

The guest only records an Unsubscribe Request (ADR 0002). The flow checks that the link exists, then inserts one Pending Request with the link&apos;s Public Id. With type-in mode on and no matching link, it inserts a Pending Request with the typed address instead. The scheduled Unsubscribe Request batch opts out the Contacts and Leads and sends the Confirmation Email.

The Pending Key allows one Pending Request per link or address, so a repeat click fails the insert. Every path, including faults, ends on the success screen so the page never reveals whether a link or address exists.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>The varRecId value without surrounding spaces. Stored as the Request&apos;s Public Id and Pending Key.</description>
        <name>linkValue</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>TRIM({!varRecId})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Pending Key of a type-in Request: E: plus the lower-case address.</description>
        <name>typeInPendingKey</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;E:&quot; &amp; LOWER(TRIM({!Email}))</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Unsubscribe Link Quick {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <isAdditionalPermissionRequiredToRun>true</isAdditionalPermissionRequiredToRun>
    <label>Unsubscribe Link Quick</label>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>CanvasMode</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>AUTO_LAYOUT_CANVAS</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>Flow</processType>
    <recordCreates>
        <description>Records a Pending Request for the link. A duplicate Pending Key fails the insert, which also ends on the success screen.</description>
        <name>Create_Link_Request</name>
        <label>Create Link Request</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <isGoTo>true</isGoTo>
            <targetReference>screenConfirmation</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <faultConnector>
            <isGoTo>true</isGoTo>
            <targetReference>screenConfirmation</targetReference>
        </faultConnector>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Pending_Key__c</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>linkValue</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Public_Id__c</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>linkValue</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Status__c</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Pending</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>Unsubscribe__c</object>
    </recordCreates>
    <recordCreates>
        <description>Records a Pending Request for the typed address. The batch decides whether the address matches a Contact or Lead. A duplicate Pending Key fails the insert, which also ends on the success screen.</description>
        <name>Create_Type_In_Request</name>
        <label>Create Type-In Request</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>screenConfirmation</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <faultConnector>
            <isGoTo>true</isGoTo>
            <targetReference>screenConfirmation</targetReference>
        </faultConnector>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Pending_Key__c</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>typeInPendingKey</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Status__c</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Pending</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Unsubscribe_Email__c</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Email</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>Unsubscribe__c</object>
    </recordCreates>
    <recordLookups>
        <description>Retrieves the Unsubscribe Link Setup record for the screen texts and the type-in and confirmation page settings. There should only be 1.</description>
        <name>Get_Unsubscribe_Link_Setup</name>
        <label>Get Unsubscribe Link Setup</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
